.TH stpncpy 3 2026\-02\-25 "Linux man\-pages (未リリース)" 
.SH 名前
stpncpy, strncpy \- fill a fixed\-size buffer with non\-null bytes from a
string, padding with null bytes as needed
.SH ライブラリ
標準 C ライブラリ (\fIlibc\fP,\~\fI\-lc\fP)
.SH 書式
.nf
\fB#include <string.h>\fP
.P
\fBchar *strncpy(\fPsize_t dsize;
\fB              char \fP\fIdst\fP\fB[restrict \fP\fIdsize\fP\fB], const char *restrict \fP\fIsrc\fP\fB,\fP
\fB              size_t \fP\fIdsize\fP\fB);\fP
\fBchar *stpncpy(\fPsize_t dsize;
\fB              char \fP\fIdst\fP\fB[restrict \fP\fIdsize\fP\fB], const char *restrict \fP\fIsrc\fP\fB,\fP
\fB              size_t \fP\fIdsize\fP\fB);\fP
.fi
.P
.RS -4
glibc 向けの機能検査マクロの要件 (\fBfeature_test_macros\fP(7)  参照):
.RE
.P
\fBstpncpy\fP():
.nf
    Since glibc 2.10:
        _POSIX_C_SOURCE >= 200809L
    Before glibc 2.10:
        _GNU_SOURCE
.fi
.SH 説明
These functions copy non\-null bytes from the string pointed to by \fIsrc\fP
into the array pointed to by \fIdst\fP.  If the source has too few non\-null
bytes to fill the destination, the functions pad the destination with
trailing null bytes.  If the destination buffer, limited by its size, isn't
large enough to hold the copy, the resulting character sequence is
truncated.  For the difference between the two functions, see RETURN VALUE.
.TP 
\fBstrncpy\fP()
It is equivalent to
.IP
.in +4n
.EX
stpncpy(dst, src, dsize), dst
.EE
.in
.TP 
\fBstpncpy\fP()
It is equivalent to
.IP
.in +4n
.EX
memset(mempcpy(dst, src, strnlen(src, dsize)), \[aq]\[rs]0\[aq],
       dsize \- strnlen(src, dsize))
.EE
.in
.SH 返り値
.TP 
\fBstrncpy\fP()
returns \fIdst\fP.
.TP 
\fBstpncpy\fP()
returns a pointer to one past the last non\-null character written, that is,
\fIdest\~+\~strnlen(src,\~n)\fP.
.SH 属性
この節で使用されている用語の説明については、 \fBattributes\fP(7) を参照。
.TS
